WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.459
Every call goes through one reader,

2
00:00:02.459 --> 00:00:06.362
built for one task in one cloud,
and it enforces five rules.

3
00:00:06.362 --> 00:00:11.325
Only declared calls: the configuration
file lists each call with its permission,

4
00:00:11.325 --> 00:00:15.325
and a call the task doesn't declare
throws before anything is sent.

5
00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:17.043
Reads only: it sends GET,

6
00:00:17.043 --> 00:00:21.475
and runs only the directory Get
cmdlets the call list names.

7
00:00:21.475 --> 00:00:24.955
One host: every URL,
including every next link,

8
00:00:24.955 --> 00:00:30.975
must be on the cloud's own Graph or Resource
Manager host, or the token isn't sent.

9
00:00:30.975 --> 00:00:36.225
One tenant: a live run refuses a session
in another cloud or another tenant.

10
00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:39.562
And every page: collections
are read to the end.

11
00:00:39.562 --> 00:00:41.537
One permission deserves a note.

12
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:46.242
The inventory holds Directory dot Read dot
All only because Microsoft Learn's page

13
00:00:46.242 --> 00:00:51.151
for listing delegated permission grants
names it as the least-privileged permission.

14
00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:55.730
It's the broadest read the inventory
holds, and that's the only reason.
